# The same walk from power-on as sync_title, with a different pair of
# characters. sync_title is Samus vs Pikachu and every fix measured against it
# risks being a fix for that lineup: a bone table, a hurtbox count, an
# article, a special move, a per-character data conversion. This case exists
# so that a change that helps one lineup and breaks another is visible as a
# failure rather than as nothing.
#
#   tools/pc_lockstep.py sync_pair2 --cpu 9,9 --frames 3000 --headless
#
# The character-select route below was generated with
#
#   tools/pc_route.py plan SAMUS DONKEY --lag 0
#
# and it lands one cell short on both axes, so what it actually selects is
# **Mewtwo (p0, char 16) and Fox (p1, char 1)**. That is recorded rather than
# corrected because the pair only has to differ from sync_title's, and the
# route that aims true (--lag 5, the measured stick latency) has not been
# calibrated: read p0.char/p1.char out of a run before believing a route.
description: Mewtwo vs Fox from the title screen, in step every frame
rendezvous: 24
route_zero: 187
port_input_lag: 3
scene_skew: 4
ignore: seed
ref_input: 236:+START
ref_input: 240:-START
ref_input: 400:+START
ref_input: 404:-START
ref_input: 760:MAIN:0.5:0.0
ref_input: 768:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 820:+A
ref_input: 824:-A
ref_input: 950:+A
ref_input: 954:-A
ref_input: 1000:P2:+A
ref_input: 1004:P2:-A
ref_input: 1060:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1091:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1101:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1126:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1136:+A
ref_input: 1140:-A
ref_input: 1196:P2:MAIN:1.0:0.5
ref_input: 1220:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1230:P2:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1261:P2:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1271:P2:+A
ref_input: 1275:P2:-A
ref_input: 1340:+START
ref_input: 1344:-START
ref_input: 1420:MAIN:0.5:1.0
ref_input: 1452:MAIN:0.5:0.5
ref_input: 1480:+A
ref_input: 1484:-A
